Sval: remove a search engine Sval ships for good

Firefox only hides an application provided engine on removal, because the
configuration lists it again at every load. Sval's configuration is its own,
so the search service keeps the ids the user removed and leaves them out of
the configuration it loads. Settings gives every engine row a remove button,
disabled for a default engine.

